/-!
# Real-analytic Eisenstein series on `ℍ` for `Γ₀(N)`

For a level `N : ℕ`, a point `z ∈ ℍ`, and a real parameter `s > 1`, the **real-analytic
Eisenstein series at the cusp `∞` for `Γ₀(N)`** is
$$E_N(z, s) = \sum_{\gamma \in \Gamma_\infty \backslash \overline{\Gamma}_0(N)}
  (\operatorname{Im}(\gamma z))^s,$$
where `\overline{\Gamma}_0(N) = Gamma0Projective N` is the image of `Γ₀(N)` in `PSL(2, ℤ)` and
`Γ_∞ = ⟨T⟩` is the projective stabilizer of `∞`.

By the explicit 2-to-1 bijection between cosets of `Γ_∞` in `\overline{\Gamma}_0(N)` and primitive
integer pairs `(c, d) ∈ ℤ²` with `N ∣ c`, followed by Möbius inversion on `gcd(d, N) = 1`, the
level-`N` Eisenstein series is expressed as a finite linear combination of rescaled values of the
lattice Epstein zeta function `Z(z, s)` from `EpsteinZeta.lean`:
$$2 \zeta(2 s) \left(\sum_{r \mid N} \mu(r) r^{-2 s}\right) E_N(z, s)
  = \sum_{r \mid N} \mu(r) (N r)^{-s} Z\!\left(\frac{N}{r} z,\, s\right).$$
Passing to `s → 1⁺` and using Dedekind's index formula
`[SL₂(ℤ) : Γ₀(N)] = N ∏_{p ∣ N} (1 + 1 / p)` gives the classical residue
$$\lim_{s \to 1^+} (s - 1)\, E_N(z, s) = \frac{3}{\pi\, [SL_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_0(N)]}.$$

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.pslTSubgroup`: the subgroup `⟨T⟩ ≤ PSL(2, ℤ)` generated by `T`.
* `TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.realAnalyticEisensteinSummand`: the summand `q ↦ (Im (q⁻¹ • z)) ^ s`.
* `TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.realAnalyticEisenstein`: the non-holomorphic Eisenstein series
  `E_N(z, s)` at `∞` for `Γ₀(N)`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.realAnalyticEisenstein_smul`: `Γ₀(N)`-invariance of `E_N(·, s)`.
* `TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.realAnalyticEisenstein_le_one` and
  `TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.realAnalyticEisenstein_one_le_realAnalyticEpstein`: comparison
  `0 ≤ E_N(z, s) ≤ E_1(z, s) ≤ Z(z, s)`.
* `TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.tendsto_sub_one_mul_realAnalyticEisenstein`:
  `lim_{s → 1⁺} (s - 1) E_N(z, s) = 3 / (π * [SL₂(ℤ) : Γ₀(N)])`.

## References

* [H. Iwaniec, *Spectral methods of automorphic forms*][iwaniec2002], Chapter 3.
* [D. Bump, *Automorphic forms and representations*][bump1997], §1.6.
-/

